WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.080
Good morning Hank; it’s Monday. On Thursday
I’m going to be reading and signing in Plainfield,

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.129
Indiana, and then on Friday I’m moving to
the Netherlands for two months. I keep meaning

00:00:06.129 --> 00:00:08.700
to mention to you that I’m moving to the
Netherlands for two months, but there is so

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.469
much going on! In a related story, the sound
that my anxiety makes is AAAAAAAAHHHHH!

00:00:12.469 --> 00:00:15.870
And Hank, when I get stressed out I like to
play “Google auto-fill once again proves

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.770
that people are weird”. Hank, today I’m
going to answer the questions people ask Google

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:19.930
the most beginning “Is my b...?”

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:24.740
“Is my boyfriend gay?” Huh. I wonder if
“is my hus” stars similarly. Yes. What

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:28.480
about “is my wife”-- Nope, the first two
questions we have about our wives: are they

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.430
cheating, and what is their tax status? And
people say men aren’t romantic, Hank. Similarly,

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:36.751
homosexuality never comes up if you Google
“is my g”, all we want to know is that

00:00:36.751 --> 00:00:41.120
our girlfriends are not cheating, not crazy,
and that our guns are not stolen. Off topic,

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.970
Hank, but the Venn diagrammatical intersection
between people who Google “is my girlfriend

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:48.680
cheating?” and people who Google “is my
gun stolen"? Worrisome.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:52.030
Right, but about your possibly gay boyfriend,
two things. First, human sexuality is not

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:56.550
an either/or proposition, and trying to deny
its complexity is going to make both you and

00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:01.120
your partner miserable. Secondly, let me submit
that this is not a question for Google. It

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.080
is a question for your boyfriend!

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:06.210
“Is my baby sick?” Listen, I know why
you’re asking Google this question. You’re

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:09.640
asking because the alternative is to put a
thermometer in your baby’s rectum, and your

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.760
baby will look up at you like “I am not
enjoying this!” and you’ll be like “You

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.850
know what, this isn’t my idea of a fun Thursday
night either!” and then your baby’ll be

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:21.350
like “But I am incapable of empathy!”
But it is my sad duty to inform you that while

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:25.560
Google can take a picture of your house, it
cannot stick a thermometer inside your baby’s

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.870
bottom. That’s your job, sorry. If your
baby’s under six weeks old and has a temperature

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:31.000
over a hundred and one, call your doctor immediately.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.700
“Is my boyfriend cheating on me?” Yes.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.590
“Is my baby teething?” Yes.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:38.110
“Is my boyfriend losing interest?” Well
yeah, otherwise, why would he be cheating

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:39.110
on you?

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:42.030
“Is my boyfriend cheating on me quiz?”
You want a quiz? Okay, here is your quiz:

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:46.120
Did you just Google "is my boyfriend cheating
on me?" If you answered yes, he may or may

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:50.141
not be cheating on you, but there is definitely
a problem! It may be that your boyfriend is

00:01:50.141 --> 00:01:53.420
cheating on you, or that he’s untrustworthy,
or that you’re incapable of trust, or that

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:57.130
you don’t believe that you’re good enough
to deserve his monogamous affection. It may

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:00.720
be that you feel undervalued or that he feels
smothered, but something has gone wrong that

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:05.970
Google cannot answer! You have to talk to
your boyfriend. And sometimes those conversations

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:09.990
will result in breaking up, and I know that
breaking up sucks, but it is better than having

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:12.280
to Google “is my husband cheating”!

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:16.390
“Is my baby a boy or a girl?” Probably
a boy. I mean, it’s a slight probably, but

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:17.420
I’m going with it.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:21.290
“Is my boyfriend cheating?” Come on, seriously?
We just went over this!

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:24.970
“Is my blood pressure high?” Probably,
you’re very anxious about your boyfriend,

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:28.590
and that cannot be good for your health! Ideally
you want your blood pressure to be in the

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:33.010
green or the yellow, not in the orange or
the red. Yet another example, Hank, of why

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.170
it’s good to be green.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:38.250
And lastly, “Is my baby sleeping too much?”
Okay first off, if your baby is eating enough

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:42.860
and gaining weight, your baby is not sleeping
too much. Second off, don’t take this personally,

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:43.860
but I hate you.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:47.100
So Nerdfighters with boyfriends and girlfriends,
talk to each other! Hank, don’t forget to

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.060
be awesome. I gotta go upstairs and pack;
I will see you on Wednesday!

